  "body": "**Blocked by:** #91, #82, #83\n\n## Context\n\nThis single implementation issue delivers the complete `tasks-time-fix` batch.\n\n## Task\n\nImplement pure deriveTaskTime(timeFrom,timeTo): string|null with zero-padded 24-hour HH:MM; both become HH:MM–HH:MM using en dash, one becomes that value, neither NULL. Whenever a Tasks create/patch touches either source, derive from the effective post-write pair and store time in the same generic choke-point transaction. Keep time system-owned/locked and reject direct writes. Add idempotent stale-row backfill.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Task deliverables, migrations, integration, tests, and necessary documentation.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- No UI/localized stored format or schema ownership/type change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Create/update covers both/from-only/to-only/neither exact values.\n- Changing/clearing sources recomputes atomically.\n- Direct time writes remain rejected.\n- Backfill corrects stale rows and rerun is no-op.\n",
